cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the experimental data, please cite it as below."
title: "SRAFT: Lightweight Distributed Device Authentication and Software Attestation for IoT Devices Based on Physical Unclonable Functions"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, test-campaign orchestration and raw experimental data
  for SRAFT, a lightweight distributed protocol for PUF-based device authentication
  and software attestation in local IoT networks without a continuously reachable
  trusted authority. SRAFT shards each device's Challenge-Response Pair set across
  multiple Verifiers, elects a Coordinator via Raft that never stores full CRP data,
  and gates Coordinator eligibility behind distributed software attestation.
